# ForgeMaster — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in if you want to run against a Supabase project:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# BOTH variables are OPTIONAL. With either one missing, `src/services/supabaseClient.ts` returns
# `null` and the whole app runs exactly as it does today: profiles in localStorage, no accounts,
# no clans, no network calls. That is the supported default — the public GitHub Pages build can
# ship with no backend configured at all.
#
# Only `VITE_`-prefixed variables are exposed to the client by Vite. Anything you put here WILL
# end up in the built JS bundle, so nothing secret belongs in this file.

# Supabase project URL, e.g. https://abcdefghijklmnop.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase "anon" (publishable) key.
#
# This key is PUBLIC BY DESIGN. It identifies the project and grants no privileges of its own:
# every read and write is authorised by Row Level Security policies in Postgres (see
# docs/BACKEND_PLAN.md §3/§4). Shipping it in the bundle is exactly what it is for.
#
# ⚠️ NEVER put the `service_role` (or any other secret) key here, in any other `.env*` file, or in
# a `VITE_*` variable anywhere. It bypasses RLS entirely, and a `VITE_*` value is compiled into a
# public JavaScript file served to every visitor. Server-side-only keys belong in GitHub Actions
# secrets or a server environment, never in this repo.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI note: the keep-alive workflow (.github/workflows/keepalive.yml) reads the same project from
# the repository secrets SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_ANON_KEY (unprefixed — they are never bundled).
# It exits quietly when they are not set, so forks stay green.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
